{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Noah did according to all, etc.</b> Rashi explained: 'this refers to his entry into the ark,' end quote. But if this was the intent, it would not have been necessary to say so, for the verse speaks at full length: (Genesis 7:7) ״וַיָּבֹא נֹחַ וְגוֹ׳ אֶל הַתֵּבָה״ etc., and it is written (Genesis 7:13): ״בְּעֶצֶם הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה בָּא נֹחַ״." "<b>Rather,</b> the intent of the verse is that he took of every clean beast seven by seven, and of the clean fowl seven by seven — which HaShem had commanded him in the preceding passage. Also, one may precisely note the word <b>כְּכֹל</b> to allude to the expression כֹּל mentioned in the command of HaShem. And this interpretation is well supported, for you will find that among all who entered the ark, it did not mention seven by seven of clean beasts or of the fowl of the heaven but rather two by two — so that according to appearances it would seem he did not fulfill the command of HaShem who told him seven by seven. Therefore the verse comes to inform us that he did according to all that HaShem had commanded him, and took seven by seven, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:02.324697754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}